C={741:('teaching assembly',['teaching community'],['teaching assembly','teaching seat','teaching community','assembly under a teacher'],'A teaching assembly is the community gathered under a presiding lineage figure and the public seat around which it forms.','Biographies say that people arrive there, spend successive summers there, or make it flourish; the phrase names an active teaching community, not merely a piece of furniture.'),742:('the final phrase',['the last line'],['final phrase','last phrase','final saying','last word'],'The final phrase is the demanded last verbal turn by which an encounter or career is brought to its decisive close.','Teachers ask how it is spoken, say it is where participants emerge, or pair it with departure and death; the formula remains a public demand, not a supplied universal answer.'),743:('pay respect',['make a formal bow'],['pay respects','make obeisance','bow formally','prostrate'],'To pay respect is to perform a formal bodily salutation before a person, image, or memorial.','Buddha cases and encounter records place the bow before or after a turn, so its timing is part of the recorded public action rather than an unreported inward attitude.'),744:('the Snow Mountains youth',['the youth in the Snow Mountains'],['Snow Mountains youth','Himalayan youth','youth who sought half a verse','snow mountain boy'],'The Snow Mountains youth is the pre-Chan figure who gives up his body to obtain the remaining half of a verse.','Teachers raise the sacrifice in questions, memorial prose, and comparisons with Huike’s severed arm; this is the figure’s Zen deployment, not a detached life story.'),745:('the three mysteries',['Linji’s three mysteries'],['three mysteries','Linji three mysteries','three profound gates','three mysteries and three essentials'],'The three mysteries are Linji’s named threefold sentence structure, in which each mystery is said to contain three essentials.','Later houses quote, challenge, and combine the set with guest-host, illumination-action, and other lineage vocabularies without agreeing on one explanatory paraphrase.'),746:('at those words',['upon hearing the words'],['at the words','upon those words','immediately at the saying','on hearing it'],'At those words marks the point at which a recorded consequence follows a particular utterance.','Biographies attach understanding, awakening, or acceptance to the immediately preceding speech; the phrase locates the narrated turn and does not by itself define what was understood.'),747:('the seven buddhas',['seven buddhas of the past'],['seven Buddhas','seven past Buddhas','seven Buddha lineage','rites of the seven Buddhas'],'The seven buddhas are the inherited group preceding and including Shakyamuni that Chan records place at the head of the transmitted line.','Masters cite their verse lineage, ritual forms, halls, and Manjushri’s relation to them, bringing the group into present questions rather than offering seven separate biographies.'),748:('the host',['the proprietor'],['host','proprietor','person in charge','guest and host'],'The host is the person who owns, governs, or occupies the controlling side of a place or encounter.','Records contrast host with guest, ask someone to act as host, or describe the host’s standing; longer 主人公 compounds were excluded so they do not silently redefine this bare word.'),749:('release from the summer retreat',['close the summer residence'],['end summer retreat','summer retreat release','close the summer retreat','release from summer residence'],'Release from the summer retreat is the formal close of the fixed summer residence.','Records use it as a dated heading for small or full assemblies and contrast the unchanged participants with the passing of the retreat period.'),750:("cut off everyone’s tongue",['silence every speaker'],['cut off every tongue','silence everyone','leave no one able to speak','stop the world’s tongues'],"To cut off everyone’s tongue is to leave all other speakers without a viable reply or verbal opening.",'Comments apply the hyperbolic bodily image to a turn, departure, blow, or wall-facing stance whose handling is said to pre-empt the field; it reports a public verdict, not literal mutilation.')}
